# Paths the prose judge skips, one per line, each starting with a slash and
# read as relative to the repository root.
#
# A quiz sheet is not documentation. Its readers are a pub quiz team, sitting at
# a table mid-round with a pen, deciding what to write in the gap; and the
# quizmaster, reading questions and answers aloud to a room. They are playing a
# game, not learning how something works. The lines are questions, answers and
# playing instructions, so the prose rules for exposition do not apply to them:
# a question withholds its answer on purpose, and an instruction repeats itself
# on purpose, because it is heard once across a noisy room.
/quizzes
/FUTURE-QUIZ-ROUNDS.md
